                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Kingdom Rush Frontiers is proof that a tower defense game can make you feel like a tactical genius and a complete idiot in the same five minutes. You place your towers with the confidence of a seasoned general, and then a pack of desert bandits strolls past your carefully planned defense like it's a casual afternoon walk.\nThe desert setting is a breath of fresh air, with new enemies, new maps, and new tricks that force you to rethink everything you learned. Upgrading towers is dangerously satisfying, and picking the right heroes feels like assembling the Avengers, if the Avengers were a wizard, a pirate, and a very angry warrior with questionable fashion choices.\nThe art is bright and charming, the humor is sharp, and the difficulty has that perfect \"just one more try\" bite. Three stars on every level? Sure, I'll just casually give up my free time and my sanity. 10/10, my towers have defended more bravely than I ever have in real life.",
